    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1226">

                <pb facs="1165" n="1153" xml:id="pg1153"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">833.00/671: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in Uruguay</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Wilson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-05-31T16:00:00-04:00">May 31, 1940—4 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>46. Your 88, May 30, 10 a.m. Please keep the Department closely informed by
                    telegram of any developments.</p>
                <p>By order of the President the heavy cruiser <hi rendition="#italic">Quincy</hi>
                    now off Guantanamo has been instructed to proceed immediately to Rio de Janeiro
                    and from there directly to Montevideo for “friendly visits of courtesy”. You
                    will be informed subsequently by telegram of the date of arrival.</p>
                <p>I think it would be well for you to consider, possibly in consultation with the
                    appropriate members of the government, any special arrangements which could be
                    made to give significance to the call of the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Quincy.</hi></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
